00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:25,000
OK, and to kind of wind it up,

151
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,280
And because I really love the history of these sorts of things.

152
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:31,080
Before I play this, though, here's a couple of things

153
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,680
that will help you understand it better.

154
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,480
Bill is now married.

155
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:38,800
He actually married one of the secretaries at the BSA offices.

156
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,200
Her name is Grace

157
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:45,320
And they are living at the Schiff Scout Reservation in New Jersey

158
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:49,320
And Bill has established a troop- troop number one in New Jersey

159
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:53,840
And he's using that troop kind of his his lab- to develop things.

160
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:56,920
Anyway, that'll just help you understand a couple of things in this story.

161
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:00,600
Let's let Bill explain for a little while his relationship

162
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:04,040
with Baden Powell, the founder of Scouting.

163
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,160
He knew Baden Powell

164
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:11,640
In 1935, Baden Powell and this wife who was the chief girl scout.

165
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:16,160
they took a trip around the world and they had planned to be at the

166
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:19,720
First National Jamboree we had in 1935.

167
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:24,560
The one that was canceled because of the polio outbreak in Virginia.

168
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:27,000
And then he came out to the Schiff Scout Reservation.

169
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,640
So I had Baden Powell and Lady Baden Powell in my house

170
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:33,080
And we had a wonderful time with breakfast and so on.

171
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:38,520
But then what happened was that we went to the Jamboree and Holland in 1937.

172
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:42,440
When we got out there and out that the whole hotel has been taken over

173
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,360
by the British Jamboree contingent staff,

174
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:48,200
Next morning we, as we opened the door-

175
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:53,000
How's another one of these complete coincidence of meeting the right people

176
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,760
at the right time, Lady Baden Powell and Baden Powell

177
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,080
coming up the corridor.

178
00:10:57,080 --> 00:11:00,439
They had just arrived from England and they just come to the hotel

179
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:05,040
And Lady Baden Powell saw them, saw us, and said: Oh, it's Bill and Grace.

180
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,439
And he said: Well, have you had your breakfast?

181
00:11:07,439 --> 00:11:09,360
No, we haven't had our breakfast.

182
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:12,000
Well, you just wait a while until we get ourselves settled.

183
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:15,640
So the two hillcourts had breakfast with the two big powers.

184
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:18,960
So, and on the basis of that, of course they are right.

185
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:22,600
So he came to the point of getting so close to Lady Baden Powell

186
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:26,000
that when I wanted to take Baden Powell's books

187
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,560
and transform them into World Brotherhood editions

188
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:34,040
for starting scouting up again around the world after the World War,

189
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:38,200
he gave me a permission to just take Baden Powell's book and edit them

190
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:43,040
And they are now the official versions of the Baden Powell Scouting for Boys

191
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,240
and Asian Scout Masters.

192
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:47,680
So there's the basis of a very close relationship

193
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:50,280
between the Baden Powell's and the hillcourts.

194
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:55,160
And Baden Powell passes away in 1941, just a few years after this meeting.

195
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:58,199
As Bill explained, he becomes the editor

196
00:11:58,199 --> 00:12:01,319
of the official publications of Baden Powell's works

197
00:12:01,319 --> 00:12:03,439
after the Second World War,

198
00:12:03,439 --> 00:12:06,319
And I know this is unraveling a little bit like a mystery.

199
00:12:06,319 --> 00:12:08,439
but look at all the connections.

200
00:12:08,439 --> 00:12:11,680
One of the original scouts in 1910 in Denmark becomes

201
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:14,720
the voice of the Boy Scouts of America,

202
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,120
has a relationship with the founder of Scouting

203
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:21,720
that is close enough to allow him to edit his works.

204
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,600
So where is the source code?

205
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,360
Where exactly is it expressed?

206
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,800
Well, Bill has an answer for that

207
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:33,920
And it comes in his answer to this question.

208
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,560
What do you think Baden Powell would say?

209
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,880
What was his point in doing all that?

210
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:43,440
Well, I think what he would do is he would pretty well have page nine

211
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:48,320
in mind, because that was completely based upon Baden Powell.

212
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:52,120
And what trouble writing that page and any other page,

213
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:55,680
Because I wanted on one page to be able to say:

214
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,800
well, this is what Scouting is all about.

215
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:00,000
This is the wonderful life you would have in Scouting.

216
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,840
You will learn a lot of different skills,

217
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:07,560
You will meet good friends and you will have a chance to even learn leadership and so on.

218
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:12,040
And we're going to need real leaders

219
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:15,079
with that kind of a spirit in the future,

220
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:18,439
and even more than we have ever needed them before.

221
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:21,880
In order to do that, you have to show the example of that,

222
00:13:22,199 --> 00:13:26,480
because you have to take on the role model of becoming a good scout,

223
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,719
living up to the scout oath and the scout law

224
00:13:28,719 --> 00:13:31,240
and following all of the principles of Scouting.

225
00:13:31,599 --> 00:13:34,240
If you get yourself really involved in all of these things-

226
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:36,880
and that's the important thing, getting yourself involved-

227
00:13:37,079 --> 00:13:39,480
Don't be a passive person there

228
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:43,200
and then step in and help other people at all times.

229
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:46,120
You see, that's another part of the scout idea,

230
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:49,240
because he believed in all people getting together

231
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:51,600
and helping each other in a real friendship.

232
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:54,200
So I think he will stick to this general idea.

233
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,800
Of course, that's right out of it now.

234
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,160
So now we know where the source code is.

235
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:02,080
It's on page nine. page nine of what you ask.

236
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:05,560
Well, I'm going to tell you, but think about this

