00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,360
Why did he do all this in the first place?

241
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,400
Well, Bill says it's on page nine.

242
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:21,480
Here's a guy who's got this tremendous amount of writing

243
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,400
that he's done over his lifetime

244
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,440
And he says this was the most challenging page I ever wrote,

245
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,480
because he wanted to boil it down

246
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,920
to the source code of Scouting.

247
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:35,720
To better explain how page nine came to be,

248
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:40,360
we need to understand what happened in the early 1970s

249
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,480
that brought Bill out of retirement,

250
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,920
where he donated a year of his time

251
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:47,600
to rewrite the Scouting handbook.

252
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:50,400
What you're going to hear is Bill speaking

253
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:55,000
in a video, actually, that I've shared on the blog before

254
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,840
And I'll have a link to that video in the post

255
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,440
that contains this podcast, where he's visiting

256
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:02,440
with some Scouts and Scouters in Florida in 1987.

257
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,760
And he explains what happened

258
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:07,320
and how he ended up coming up with page nine

259
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,000
And, by way of explanation

260
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,200
to preface what Bill's going to say,

261
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,800
give you a little context here.

262
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,600
So in the early 1970s,

263
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:17,560
the Boy Scouts of America initiates a study of Scouting

264
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,800
that has some what will become

265
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:23,000
pretty much disastrous results

266
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:26,080
And Bill tells us a little bit about that

267
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:28,080
and his reaction to it.

268
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:31,240
It had to be brought up to date.

269
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,840
That was a big thing in those days

270
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,640
And it had to be relevant.

271
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,560
So they came up with a suggestion

272
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,440
that we should change it completely.

273
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:42,160
There's too much emphasis about the outer doors,

274
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:43,600
The people in the National

275
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,200
Architectural Development stuff,

276
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,840
that we started lowering all the expectations

277
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:50,000
or whatever first class Scouts should be.

278
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,400
He didn't have to be an outdoorsman,

279
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,560
As a matter of fact, when we started the Skill Award.

280
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:55,560
you only had to take three Skill Awards

281
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:58,560
for ten to put three Skill Awards in a second class.

282
00:15:58,560 --> 00:15:59,560
three Skill Awards,

283
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,080
You could pick your own.

284
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,720
And I insisted that we should have at least hiking

285
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,280
and for second class

286
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:07,040
and we should have camping for first class,

287
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:08,920
because this idea of becoming first class

288
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:11,120
without having a camp was rather silly.

289
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:15,000
That's why the membership went down from six million

290
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,320
to more than a half million.

291
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,760
Then I started to wonder:

292
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,400
is the Boy Scouts sales going down

293
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,560
Because my last handbook that came out

294
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:27,880
up until 1970 was selling 600,000 copies a year.

295
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:31,480
In seven years it had dropped to about 340,000.

296
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:32,720
And the same is going down

297
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,200
because the membership is going down?

298
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:37,160
Or is it the other way around,

299
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,760
that the membership is going down

300
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:40,240
because a Boy Scout handbook

301
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,800
doesn't tell the story

302
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,439
about how much excitement you can have as a scout?

303
00:16:44,439 --> 00:16:47,360
So I decided to put a year of my life on the line

304
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,720
and I suggested to them

305
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:51,040
I'll write you another Boy Scout handbook for your job.

306
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,600
That Boy Scout handbook came out

307
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:55,800
on the 8th of February 1979..

308
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,600
Will you open the page?

309
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,440
What edition is it?

310
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,600
What printing is it? sir?

311
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,600
I believe this one is the ninth edition,

312
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:05,040
And will you see how many have been printed

313
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,040
on that particular edition,

314
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,240
No ninth edition.

315
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,440
Three million four million fifty thousand.

316
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,160
How many?

317
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,000
Three million four million fifty thousand.

318
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,440
We have printed more than three million copies

319
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:20,640
of this since this book came out.

320
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,560
Will you turn to page nine

321
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:28,560
in all of your books

322
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,400
When you go home?

323
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,120
I don't want you to do it right here,

324
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:34,000
But the thing that's happening out in your camp.

325
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,480
we have a training group there of 64 men

326
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,440
from all over this whole region

327
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:43,080
And there are 17 leaders,

328
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:45,800
including the National Director of Boy Scouting,

329
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,600
the National Director of Training,

330
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,480
the National Director of Research.

331
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,720
They're part of the training group out here

332
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:54,760
because the Hillcourt has been yelling

333
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:58,240
about the fact that Scoutmasters should be trained

334
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:01,800
to make every single promise on page nine

335
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:05,080
come true in the lives of your kids.

336
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,640
So that recording. there was a lot of noise in it

337
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,600
and I did my best.

338
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,360
I'm not an audio engineer, obviously,

339
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:14,040
but I did my best to clean it up a little bit

340
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:16,040
and it may be a little difficult to understand.

341
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,600
So let me reiterate:

342
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,200
This study happens.

343
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,840
The Scouting program changes radically

344
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:24,200
because they want to update everything

345
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:28,160
and they think, oh, this outdoor stuff is old hat,

346
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,880
Boys aren't attracted to that,

347
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:31,720
And so we're gonna change things around

348
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:34,200
and we're gonna make it more theoretical,

349
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:38,040
We're going to try and make things more palatable.

350
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:41,080
We're gonna get rid of a lot of this outdoor emphasis.

351
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:44,000
So Bill volunteers a year of his time

352
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,880
to rewrite the Scout Handbook in the late 70s,

353
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,600
and the product of that year

354
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,760
is the ninth edition of the Boy Scout Handbook.

355
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:53,280
And on the mysterious page nine- that's where it is-

356
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:56,440
It's in the ninth edition of the Boy Scout Handbook

357
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:59,280
And, as we've learned through all the connections

358
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:03,160
through this series, there's the source code of Scouting.

359
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:06,480
So what is on page nine?

360
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:10,120
What did the voice of the Boy Scouts of America,

361
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,680
the guy who knew Baden Powell,

362
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:14,520
the guy who became a Scout just about as soon

363
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,680
as anybody in the world could become a Scout

364
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,560
And who wrote about Scouting for his entire life?

365
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,680
what was the most challenging thing for him to do

366
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,760
was to reduce it to one page,

367
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:26,280
and it's page nine of the ninth edition

368
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,240
of the Boy Scout Handbook.

369
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:30,560
So what exactly does that page say?

370
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,320
I'm gonna read it to you right now,

371
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:33,920
because it's a quick read,

372
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,560
and it's titled Your Life as a Scout.

373
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,880
You're an American boy

374
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,400
and before long you'll be an American man.

375
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:42,920
It's an important to America and to yourself

376
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:45,480
that you become a citizen of fine character,

377
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:49,400
physically strong, mentally awake and morally straight.

378
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,920
Boy Scouting will help you become that kind of citizen.

379
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:55,520
but also Scouting will give you fellowship and fun.

380
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,280
Yes, it's fun to be a Boy Scout.

381
00:19:57,280 --> 00:20:00,560
It's fun to go hiking and camping with your best friends,

382
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:03,840
to swim, to dive, to paddle a canoe, to wield an axe,

383
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,800
to follow the footsteps of the pioneers

384
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,960
who led the way through the wilderness,

385
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:10,320
to stare into the glowing embers of a campfire

386
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:12,360
and dream the wonders of the life

387
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:14,080
that is in store for you.

388
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:17,600
It's also fun to learn to walk noiselessly through the woods,

389
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:21,040
to stalk close to a grazing deer without being noticed,

390
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:24,320
to bring a bird close to you by imitating its call.

391
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:28,460
It's fun to find your way, cross country by map and compass,

392
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:29,919
to make a meal when you're hungry,

393
00:20:29,919 --> 00:20:32,040
to take a safe swim when you're hot,

394
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,919
to make yourself comfortable for the night

395
00:20:33,919 --> 00:20:36,240
in a tent under the stars.

396
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:39,080
In Scouting you become an outdoorsman.

397
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:42,679
but Scouting is far more than fun in the outdoors,

398
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:44,480
hiking and camping.

399
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,480
Scouting is a way of life.

400
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:49,720
Scouting is growing into a responsible manhood,

401
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:52,720
learning to be of service to others.

402
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:55,080
The Scout Oath and the Scout Law

403
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:57,320
are your guides to citizenship.

404
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:59,800
They tell you what is expected of a Scout.

405
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,720
They point out your duties.

406
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:05,280
The Scout motto is: be prepared-

407
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:07,400
prepared to take care of yourself

408
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,760
and to help other people in need.

409
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:13,120
The Scout slogan is: do a good turn daily

410
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:16,760
Together. the motto and slogan spell out your ability

411
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:19,200
and your willingness to serve.

412
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:23,000
Your life as a Scout will make you strong and self-reliant.

413
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,760
You'll learn Scoutcraft skills

414
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:26,920
that will benefit you as you grow

415
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,040
and in time, you'll develop the skills

416
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,800
of leadership as well.

417
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:33,640
So pitch in, swing into action

418
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,520
In your patrol and your troop.

419
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:37,920
you'll have some of the best times of your life.

420
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,680
I can't put it any better.

421
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,680
I doubt anybody could.

422
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:44,480
What a wonderful challenge

423
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:46,080
and what a wonderful description

424
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:48,280
of exactly what Scouting is,

425
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,280
The DNA of Scouting, the source code of Scouting.

426
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:52,920
Scouting is fun in the outdoors,

427
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:55,480
but it's more than just that fun.

428
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,680
It is a way of life

429
00:21:57,680 --> 00:22:00,880
that you'll grow into, a responsible human being.

430
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,880
That's the source code,

431
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,880
That's what we need to be thinking about,

432
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,280
That's what we need to understand

433
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:10,240
and we need to apply as Scouters

434
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:13,040
to serve the youth that we're serving.

435
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,600
Wherever you are in the world, it's gonna work.

436
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,280
However, things have changed and morphed

437
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:21,639
and gotten different in our cultures and societies,

438
00:22:21,639 --> 00:22:24,000
the source code is still going to work.

439
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,800
However much training and policy and procedure

440
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:29,840
and organizational craziness there is out there,

441
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:34,240
the source code is still going to work.

442
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:38,000
That's what Scouting really is.

443
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:41,160
Now take that, take that page nine,

444
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:45,400
take that source code and make it a reality.

445
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:49,040
That's what Bill said. he wants Scouters to be trained

446
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:52,760
to make those things a reality in the lives of their Scouts.

447
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:55,500
He understands and he explains to the Scouts

448
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:57,880
that, yes, this is going to be a lot of fun

449
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,740
and it's challenging and it's gonna be great,

450
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:01,480
but there's an ulterior motive,

451
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:02,940
because it's a way of life

452
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:06,180
that helps you grow into a responsible human being.

453
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:07,620
There's no secret code.

454
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:11,360
there's no step one, two, three. for Scouters,

455
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:14,320
The challenge is to take that page nine

456
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:17,020
and make it a reality in the life of your Scouts.

457
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:21,340
and it's simple. it's very, very simple

458
00:23:21,340 --> 00:23:23,540
And I'm reminded of something that Baden Powell said:

459
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:26,180
it's like swinging a scythe or a golf club:

460
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:28,980
Very, very simple. anybody can do it,

461
00:23:28,980 --> 00:23:32,620
but it takes a lifetime of practice to get good at it.

462
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,140
So that's our job, that's everything that we do.

463
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:36,740
Get good at the source code,

464
00:23:36,740 --> 00:23:39,900
get good at making it happen in the lives of your Scouts.

465
00:23:39,900 --> 00:23:44,540
That's the only thing that ends up really mattering.

466
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:47,540
How to test if what you're doing as a Scouter

467
00:23:47,540 --> 00:23:52,540
is advancing the aims of Scouting is to read page nine.

468
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:54,660
Are you making that happen?

469
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:56,020
Then you're successful.

470
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:59,300
Are you realizing that ulterior motive

471
00:23:59,300 --> 00:24:02,000
in the lives of the young people you're serving?

472
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,800
Then you're successful. Scouter.

473
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:04,880
That's the source code.

474
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:08,360
It's as important as it is simple,

475
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:11,120
And it's a huge challenge for us to see

476
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:15,080
in that simplicity exactly what we're up to

477
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:17,160
and the way that Scouting works.

